    "why_it_matters": "An Ansari-family egg shop on Mall Road since 1918, converted into an omelette stall in 1975. Five generations in; Shahid Ansari runs it now. The cheese omelette pressed between two slices of white bread is the dish boarding-school kids in Mussoorie remember for decades.",
    "insider_tip": "It's a stand-up street counter, no seating. Locals get the cheese variant; ask for chilli and onion if you want it loaded. Boarders get priority on weekends.",
